Package: xios-server
Name: Xios (IOSurface X server)
Version: 1.20.11+ios3
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Depends: libxfont2, libpixman-1-0, libxau6, libxdmcp6, libiosexec1 (>= 1.3.1), libmd0, xkbcomp, xkeyboard-config, xauth
Recommends: xios-desktop-defaults
Section: X11
Priority: optional
Description: Native IOSurface X server for the Xios iOS app
 Xios is an X11 server built on xorg-server 1.20.11 (the same patched tree as
 Xvfb) with a custom IOSurface DDX: instead of a software framebuffer, it renders
 straight into a shared IOSurface that the native Xios iOS app maps into a Metal
 texture via a mach-port hand-off, a zero-copy display path (no per-frame upload).
 .
 Xios writes /var/jb/tmp/xios.json describing the surface and the rendezvous socket
 so the app picks the zero-copy path automatically; touch/keyboard come back in via
 XTEST. Xvfb remains available separately for headless/debug X11 sessions, but is not
 the app display path.
 .
 Like the rest of the stack it is rebuilt for rootless /var/jb and ad-hoc/DER signed,
 and its XKB init spawns xkbcomp via /var/jb/bin/sh so keyboard setup works with no
 on-device hacks. Ships the xios-server.sh launcher. Pair with a window manager
 (fluxbox), xterm, and the x11-fonts-sf package. Built for iPadOS/iOS rootless
 (palera1n/Dopamine).
